Replaces test/fixtures/t12-omarchy-6d7826d (the beta-2/edge pin), retired
2026-08-15 with the 4.0.0 stable rebase. What actually moved between the two:

  * Service.qml  471 -> 551 lines. Upstream added the stranded-lock recovery
    path and reworked the fingerprint/PAM flow, which shifted our blank-timer
    block from line ~373 to ~416 and rewrote the `onTriggered` body just below
    it. Patch 0010 still applies -- its context lines are byte-identical and the
    applier uses offset-tolerant `git apply` -- so this is drift, not a break.
    Classified in docs/findings/T9-stable-delta-classification.md (delta B).
  * limine.conf  UNCHANGED, byte for byte (same sha256 as at 6d7826d). Patch
    0020's target did not move at all across 127 upstream commits.

⚠️ WHEN iso/RUNTIME MOVES, THIS DIRECTORY MUST MOVE WITH IT. Refetch both
files at the new ref, rename the directory, and re-run
test/unit/test-t12-patch-applier.sh. If a shipped patch no longer applies to
the refreshed fixture that is not a test bug -- it is the seam doing its one
job, and the patch needs a rebase. The suite asserts the directory name matches
iso/RUNTIME so a stale fixture cannot sit here unnoticed.

The drift fixture for `interval: 3000` (upstream commit 35a6940, "Just 3
seconds of screen on after lock") is not stored: the suite derives it from
Service.qml by substituting the literal, which reproduces upstream's content in
that neighbourhood exactly and cannot go stale independently of the file above.
